  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Student Activity</title>
      <para>Now that you have written equations from tables, it is time to write systems of
        equations from graphs.</para>
      <para>
        <emphasis>Part 1: Writing a System of Equations from a Given Graph </emphasis>
      </para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 8, use the given graph:</para>
      <figure class="unnumbered">
        <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_06_01.jpg" />
        </media>
      </figure>

        <exercise id="_0a49b738-8436-497d-8638-18fa613b6ced" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the green dashed line what is the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 9</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 9.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ec23dfc4-4e5e-4dfc-b5a8-854b9fbd123c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the green dashed line what is the slope?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! -1</para>
            <para>The correct answer is -1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--Q#3-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the equation of the green dashed line in slope-intercept form?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(y= -x+9\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

        <exercise id="adafd334-fdb7-43a1-aa7d-69c9835cde5a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>

            <para>For the orange solid line what is the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>

            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e5b6a568-4cef-49f8-a35b-df8ac3233ff4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>

            <para>For the orange solid line what is the slope?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>

            <para>The correct answer is 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--Q#6-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the equation of the orange solid line in slope-intercept form?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(y = 3x +5\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#7-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Write the two equations as a system of linear equations.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(y= -x+9\)</para>
          <para>\(y = 3x +5\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#8-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the solution of the system of equations?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\((1, 8)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <para>
        <emphasis>Part 2: Use a Graph to Solve a Given System</emphasis>
      </para>
      <para>Now that you wrote a system of equations from a given graph, how can you work backward
        and graph a given system of equations by hand? Discuss this with a partner.</para>
      <para>For questions 1 - 2, use this system of equations:</para>
      <para>\(y=4x-4\)</para>
      <para>\(y= -2x+8\)</para>
      <!--Q#1-->

      <exercise>
          <problem>
            <!--QUESTION
            IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
            <para>On the same coordinate plane, graph \(y = 4x -4\) and \(y = -2x +8\) by hand.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
              compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_06_02.jpg" />
              </media>
            </figure>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#2-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the solution to the system of equations?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\((2, 4)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <para>For numbers 3 and 4, consider the system of equations:</para>
      <para>\(y = - \frac{3}{4}x+5\)</para>
      <para>\(y=\frac{1}{2}x-5\)</para>
      <!--Q#3-->

        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <!--QUESTION
            IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
            <para>On the same coordinate plane, graph the system of equations by hand.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
              compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_06_03.jpg" />
              </media>
            </figure>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#3-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the solution to the system of equations?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\((8, -1)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>

    <section>
      <title>Video: Graphing a System of Equations</title>
      <para>Watch the following video to learn more about writing systems of equations from graphs.</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4"
          src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/RQHhdqkJEo0?si=lGR1PpEOg-oREXv2;&amp;rel=0" />
