    <section>
      <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
      <section>
        <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
      <exercise class="RFM1">
        <problem>
          <para>Graph the following system of equations on a coordinate plane:</para>
          <para>\(y=2x +5\)</para>
          <para>\(4x-2y =10\)</para>
          <para>Find the solution.</para>
          <para>(Hint: For the second equation, solve for \(y\) first.)</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Infinitely many solutions. When the second equation is solved for \(y\), it becomes
            \(-2y =-4x=10\) then \(y = 2x +5\). Both equations are the same. So, on the graph, one
            line is on top of the other and all solutions are possible.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--End
      interaction-->
    </section>
  </section>

  <section>
    <note class="self-check">
      <para>Which of the following systems of equations is graphed:</para>
      <figure class="unnumbered">
        <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
